course: dictionary
lesson: 14947
title: Rejoice: joy and praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a word is old-fashioned or formal, the words around it give you clues. «The whole village began to rejoice when the lost boy finally came home.» Villagers are happy when a lost child comes back, so rejoice must mean to feel great joy.
explain: Rejoice is a formal word. In everyday speech people more often say celebrate or be over the moon. You will meet it more in stories, hymns and the Bible than in a chat with a friend.
explain: In church, to rejoice in God means to be glad and to praise God, as in «Rejoice in the Lord always». You will find this word in hymns and Christmas carols, such as «Rejoice! Rejoice! Emmanuel».
fact: «Rejoice» means to feel or show great joy or happiness.
fact: «Rejoicing» is the noun: «There was great rejoicing when the dragon was defeated.»
fact: Rejoice can be followed by at, in or over, as in «rejoice at the news», «rejoice in God» or «rejoice over a safe return».
fact: In church and the Bible, to rejoice in God means to be glad and praise God.
fact: Rejoice is more formal than celebrate, so you will meet it more in old stories, hymns and carols.
exercise: «The villagers began to rejoice when the lost child came home.» What does rejoice mean? | Feel tired and sleepy | Walk away quietly | *Feel and show great joy | Build a wall
exercise: Which word is the noun form of rejoice? | *rejoicing | rejoin | rejoices | rejoiced
exercise: Which phrase comes from the Bible? | Run for the hills | Shut the door quietly | Count to ten | *Rejoice in the Lord always
test: «There was great rejoicing when the dragon was defeated.» What does rejoicing mean here? | A long, quiet sleep | Great anger and shouting | *Great joy and celebration | Being lost in the woods
test: Which everyday word is an easier swap for rejoice? | shrink | forget | whisper | *celebrate
exam: Which sentence uses rejoice correctly? | *The village will rejoice when the lost boy comes home. | The rain will rejoice the pencil under the bed. | Rejoice is a cold sandwich for lunch. | Please rejoice my bag to the shop.
